NUM-25: use Eo = 1 for a curb inlet when the spread is within the gutter

getCurbInletCapture() computes the gutter flow ratio Eo with getEo(Sr, T-W, W).
When the flow spread T is narrower than the depressed gutter width W, T-W is
negative, getEo() raises a negative number to the power 2.67 and returns NaN,
the "L < Lt" test is false and the inlet captures all of the flow. When the
spread is within the gutter all flow is gutter flow, so Eo = 1 (HEC-22), as
getGutterFlowRatio() already does for grates.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-25_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
index fa52cb3..1634e25 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
@@ -1494,7 +1494,8 @@ double getCurbInletCapture(double Q, double L)
     if (a > 0.0)
     {
         Sr = Sw / Sx;
-        Eo = getEo(Sr, T-W, W);
+        if (T <= W) Eo = 1.0;    // spread is within the depressed gutter
+        else        Eo = getEo(Sr, T-W, W);
         Se = Sx + (a/W) * Eo;                              //HEC-22 Eq(4-24)
     }
 
